    {
     "id": "cice_dynamics_evp_subcycle_integrated",
     "description": "Integrated pin of the coupled momentum + classic-EVP stress ODEs over one EVP subcycle, [0, 30] s = dte = dt/ndte (3600/120): the classic-EVP stress map newp = (oldp + arlx1i*(zetax2*divu - rep_prs))*denom1 (ice_dyn_evp.F90:1584-1609) is the backward-Euler step of length dte of the relaxation ODE d(stressp)/dt = (stressp_target - stressp)/Td because arlx1i = 1/86.4 = dte/Td with Td = 2*elasticDamp*dt, so one subcycle of the Fortran is one dte of the model. Initial conditions: stressp/stressm/stress12 = the step-1 ksub-1 oldp/oldm/old12 of cice_evp_stress.csv at all 15 cells x 4 corners (the stress before the first subcycle), uvel/vvel = the velocity that subcycle used (the stress-dump uvel/vvel = the momentum dump's uold/vold). Parameter overrides: those of cice_dynamics_bgrid_pins plus the momentum forcing of the same row of cice_evp_momentum.csv -- strairx/strairy = forcex/forcey (dyn_prep2 forcex = strairxU + strtltxU, ice_dyn_shared.F90:833, with the run's identically-zero ss_tltx/ss_tlty), fcor = fm/(Umassdti*dt) (Umassdti = umass/dt, F90:812-814), hemis = sign(fm) (southern hemisphere) -- the U point local (3,1) = global U(4,4) carries no momentum row (no ice at that corner) and keeps strairx = 0, fcor = -1.4e-4. Assertions: stressp/stressm/stress12 at t = 30 s at the three interior T cells of the 3x5 domain, local (2,2..4) = global (3,5..7), corners 1-4 (36 values), against the dump's ksub-1 newp/newm/new12. The pin is NOT exact, and its tolerance is stated per assertion relative to the dumped increment: abs tolerance = 0.6*|newp - oldp| (3 significant figures), so a model that left the stresses unchanged would fail every assertion. Measured residuals are 0.001-0.46 of the increment (median ~0.08; rel 1.6e-7..1.4e-3 of the value). The difference is scheme, not physics: the Fortran evaluates the subcycle's stress target on the velocity frozen at the subcycle start and only then calls stepu, while the model integrates the stress target on the velocity evolving under the continuous momentum ODE, whose mass is the T-cell Tmass rather than the Fortran's U-cell umass (grid-stagger collapse, see README.md); the exponential-vs-backward-Euler difference itself is only arlx1i/2 = 0.6% of the increment. Not asserted, with reasons: (i) the boundary cells (i = 1, i = 3, j = 1, j = 5), where the rule's halo-copy closure replaces the Fortran's physical neighbors and the residuals reach 1-21x the increment (e.g. local (1,1) corner 1 stress12), and local (1,1) corner 3, which the Fortran leaves at exactly 0 (masked corner) while the model relaxes it toward its nonzero target; (ii) the velocities: over one subcycle the dumped uvel/vvel change by <1% and the model's continuous-limit increment does not reproduce it (at local (2,2) the uvel increment has the opposite sign, residual 1.4x the increment; vvel 0.06x), because stepu is a semi-implicit pseudo-time update with umass and an implicit vrel/Cb drag rather than the physical-time m*du/dt of the model -- a velocity pin would therefore not be informative.",
